// ============================================================
// QUERY: Cloud File Exfiltration Detection (Read vs. Copy)
// Incident: INC-2026-87241
// Table: CloudAppEvents
// Purpose: Detect targeted file downloads (exfiltration) from
//          cloud storage by distinguishing FileDownloaded events
//          (copy-out) from FileAccessed events (read in place).
//          In this incident, the attacker downloaded 3 critical files
//          in a 1-second window.
// Platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Defender XDR
// ============================================================

CloudAppEvents
| where ActionType == "FileDownloaded"
| where ObjectName contains "credential"
   or ObjectName contains "banking"
   or ObjectName contains "password"
   or ObjectName contains "vpn"
   or ObjectName contains "key"
| where Timestamp >= ago(7d)
| summarize DownloadCount = count() by AccountObjectId, ObjectName, Timestamp

// ============================================================
// INCIDENT CONTEXT:
//   - Compromised User:   m.smith@lognpacific.org
//   - User ObjectId:      fa5020a1-0d42-4839-bbfe-22db0861ced5
//   - Exfil Window:       2026-06-11 03:37:22 – 03:37:23 UTC (1 second)
//
//   FILES EXFILTRATED:
//     1. VPN-Access-Credentials.txt  (03:37:22 UTC): On-prem access
//     2. Vendor-Banking-Details.txt  (03:37:22 UTC): BEC intelligence
//     3. Book.xlsx                   (03:37:23 UTC): Financial records
//
// KEY DISTINCTION:
//   FileAccessed = opened file in place (normal user behavior)
//   FileDownloaded = copied file to local system (potential exfiltration)
//
//   These events look identical in many SIEM views. You MUST filter
//   specifically for FileDownloaded to catch exfiltration. A high volume
//   of FileDownloaded events (especially in rapid succession) or downloads
//   of files with sensitive names should trigger high-priority alerts.
//
// TUNING:
//   - Extend ObjectName filters for your org's naming conventions
//   - Add a time-window cluster to detect rapid bulk downloads (multiple
//     FileDownloaded events within 60 seconds from same AccountObjectId)
//   - Consider baselining normal download frequency per user and alerting
//     on significant deviations
//   - Scope to users with payment/finance/admin access for higher signal
// ============================================================
